## 1. Analysis & Pre-Thinking

**Core Requirements:** Provide a **New Project** entry point in the sidebar apps list (`AppsSection.vue`) and the top main menu (`MainMenu.vue`), and make the **new project modal** actually appear when triggered.

**What the codebase already has (discovery results):**
- `src/store/ui.js` already exposes `newProject` state + the `showNewProject(show)` mutation.
- `src/components/project/NewProject.vue` is a complete, self-contained form that emits `close` and calls `$ui.showNewProject(false)` on success.
- `src/components/main-menu/MainMenuItems.vue` **already renders** a `New project` item → `$ui.showNewProject(true)`. `MainMenu.vue` simply renders `<MainMenuItems />`, and `WindowsMenuItems.vue` exposes the same action. So the **menu entry point already exists**.
- **Gap #1:** `AppsSection.vue` has no "New Project" entry (its "New" item opens a *chat*, not a project).
- **Gap #2 (the real bug):** the current root `App.vue` **no longer renders** the `<NewProject>` modal. The old version did (`<modal v-if="$ui.newProject">…</modal>`), so today `$ui.showNewProject(true)` flips a flag nothing listens to — clicking "New project" does nothing.

**Strategic Approach:**
1. Add a `New Project` `NavItem` to `AppsSection.vue` that calls `$ui.showNewProject(true)`.
2. Re-mount the global `<NewProject>` modal at the app root (`App.vue`) so **every** launcher (AppsSection, MainMenuItems, WindowsMenuItems, QuickBar) works. This must be global because the launchers live outside `RouterView` and the sidebar isn't rendered in every layout (e.g. desktop portrait).

**Dependencies & Risks:** The shared `<modal>` component teleports itself to `$root.$el`, so placing it inside the logged-in branch of `App.vue` is safe and avoids duplicate modals.

**Target Files:** `src/components/layout/AppsSection.vue` (modify), `src/App.vue` (modify). `MainMenuItems.vue` needs **no change** (already correct).

## 2. Minimum Changes Approach
- **AppsSection.vue** — one `NavItem` + one handler.
- **App.vue** — one import + one global `<modal>`.

